<protocol name="hitl" type="cross_cutting" domain="creative">

## PURPOSE

Handle Human-in-the-Loop feedback for creative processing.
Load when ANY tool response contains `[HITL_FEEDBACK]` marker.

---

## CRITICAL: PM VISIBILITY

**PM cannot see HITL events directly.**

```
[User] <--HITL--> [You] --response--> [PM]
                    ^
              PM cannot see this
```

Your response format is the ONLY signal PM receives.
**Always include HITL markers in your response.**

---

## SIMPLE LOGIC

| User Says | What To Do |
|-----------|------------|
| Specific feedback | Apply it, retry (no limit) |
| Question ("why?") | Explain, resubmit same work |
| Cancel | Report to PM what was done |
| Bare reject (no info) | Go to PM - ask what's wrong |

**No escalation limits. Keep iterating until user is happy or cancels.**

---

## ACTIONABLE FEEDBACK - Apply and Retry

When user gives ANY specific direction, apply it and retry:

```
[HITL_FEEDBACK] "Make the background light gray, not white"

[HITL RESOLVED]

**User Feedback:** "Make the background light gray, not white"

**Applied:** Background white -> light gray

Proceeding with corrected processing.
-> image_studio(background_color="light_gray", ...)
```

```
[HITL_FEEDBACK] "Too dark, make it brighter"

[HITL RESOLVED]

**User Feedback:** "Too dark, make it brighter"

**Applied:** Increased brightness/exposure

Proceeding with corrected processing.
-> image_studio(lighting={...brighter settings...}, ...)
```

---

## QUESTION - Explain and Resubmit

When user asks "why" - explain your reasoning and resubmit same work:

```
[HITL_FEEDBACK] "Why did you crop so much?"

[HITL RESOLVED]

**User Feedback:** "Why did you crop so much?"

**Explanation:** Cropped to focus on product center and meet standard hero dimensions (1:1 square).

Resubmitting same work. Reject with specific instructions if you'd like different cropping.
-> write_data(...)
```

---

## CANCEL - Report to PM

When user cancels, report what was done:

```
[HITL_FEEDBACK] "Cancel" / "Never mind"

[HITL CANCELED]

**User canceled the task.**

**Work Completed:**
- 3/5 images processed
- asset_abc123 created (before cancel)

**Work Remaining:**
- 2 images not processed

Returning to PM.
```

---

## BARE REJECT - Go to PM

When user rejects without explanation, you cannot guess. Go to PM:

```
[HITL_FEEDBACK] "Reject" / "No" / (empty)

## HITL FEEDBACK REQUIRES PM DIRECTION

**User Feedback:** "Reject"

**What Was Proposed:**
- Background: White
- Style: Product-centered hero shot
- Processing: Background removal + shadow

**What I Need:** Specific feedback on what to change.

PM, please ask user what they'd like different.
```

---

## RESPONSE FORMATS

### Resolved (then CALL tool)

```
[HITL RESOLVED]

**User Feedback:** "[exact feedback]"

**Applied:** [what changed]

Proceeding with corrected action.
-> [tool_call]
```

### Canceled

```
[HITL CANCELED]

**Work Completed:** [what was done]
**Work Remaining:** [what wasn't done]

Returning to PM.
```

### Needs PM (bare reject only)

```
## HITL FEEDBACK REQUIRES PM DIRECTION

**User Feedback:** "[exact feedback]"

**What Was Proposed:** [summary]

**What I Need:** [specific question for user]
```

---

## ANTI-PATTERNS

**Wrong:** Responding without HITL marker
```
"What style would you prefer?"  # PM doesn't know this is HITL
```

**Wrong:** Describing action instead of executing
```
[HITL RESOLVED]
Proceeding with: {"background": "gray"}  # TEXT, not tool call!
```

**Correct:**
```
[HITL RESOLVED]
Proceeding with corrected action.
-> image_studio(background="gray")  <-- ACTUAL CALL
```

</protocol>
